    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAfter copying 55 MB of text, I noticed that Neovim suddenly became slower to start. Using `--startuptime`, I found:\n\n```\n438.662  432.497  432.497: sourcing /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/autoload/provider/clipboard.vim\n```\n\nProbably related:\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/9570\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/11804\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. copy 55MB of text\n2. run\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean --cmd \"set clipboard=unnamedplus\" --startuptime log\n```\n\n3. in the log file:\n\n```\n439.623  433.807  433.807: sourcing /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/autoload/provider/clipboard.vim\n```\n\nAdditionally,\n\n`:echo provider#clipboard#Executable()` shows `xsel`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo performance issue\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-008209d148\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux x86_64\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nst 0.8.5\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nst-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
